    "body": "Hi @Nadya678,\r\n\r\nThis kind of user interface question is outside the scope of the HTML spec. It's true that in some popular browsers on some platforms, certain keys trigger an element's activation behavior. But that's browser-dependent. Browsers are free to innovate in how activation behavior is triggered, and the spec doesn't constrain them; for example, some years ago someone came up with a novel new type of browser, the mobile web browser, where neither of these things are true, and instead touching the screen is what triggers activation behavior.\r\n\r\nAs such, I'll close this, since it's not something we'll be changing in the spec. But, I'm happy to continue discussing these things in the closed thread, if you'd find that helpful.",
